   "user_review": {
    "username": "caitlinrose93",
    "date": "2 years ago",
    "rating": {
     "score": 2,
     "max_score": 5
    },
    "comment": "I was disappointed greatly with my stay - I booked for 3 weeks and the pictures looked beautiful but very much youth hostel vibes - other guests constantly leaving plates and food in the sink, bathroom on middle floor stank when you walked past, despite the cleaner’s brilliant efforts every day to have kept nice, it very much was like uni halls and no one cared. My room I expected to be a lot airier from the photos however as you can see there wasn’t proper windows, the slats opened to another corrugated roof type thing, there was however a window round a corner where desk is but did not let in natural light to end area and gave the room a “cave like” feel as another guest described, again bathroom drains smelled really badly and air con wasn’t working so was constantly too hot with poor ventilation - when complained they have engineer look at it then gave me a fan, noisy and gave me a sore throat but better than the lack of sleep due to heat. Pillows - BRING YOUR OWN - 2 flat over used pillows on a king size bed, I ended up using my airplane neck pillow the full time. Walls are also PAPER thin so wouldn’t recommend unless you have earplugs and were staying solo - I had read this in other reviews but unfortunately thought they were over exaggerating (they were not).. there is also a window from middle hall to the top bedroom I was on without a blind so every time someone used hall light it shone fully through window - not ideal when the light switch is 2 flights down from you and people are working through the house to American time zone at 2am on a Wednesday!!  ||They also had workmen booked in for week 3/3 I was here - they did not mention this or offer discount. There was constant banging some days or drilling , no use of kitchen or living room facilities through day and no heads up or discount offered which would have been the reasonable thing should you wish to keep your hostel open, I went down in the morning to 2 builders offering me a coffee in the middle of the kitchen without any prior acknowledgment, I had to ask them to move so I could use washing machine, not a huge deal but as a single woman in pjs it would have been good to have a heads up. Also lost use of outdoors due to them doing a full paint job, again, without informing guests. By the end I was happy to be leaving as the lack of sleep was making me a bit ill. ||Pros - Location was good - really good actually and cleaner really good at her job - on the occasion the internet went down when I was working this was also resolved quickly. ||Overall I would say fine if young and having a quick weekend in Lisbon but if looking for a nicer setting or for any longer I wouldn’t bother - I will be glad to get to a kitchen I can use without stepping over builders having a coffee (not their fault) and a good night’s sleep!",
    "link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Hotel_Review-g189158-d15634225-r940468535?m=68573&staydates=2026_11_15_2026_11_16&uguests=1_2_0&supdv=desktop&supuc=US&supul=en"
   },
